  "summary_en": "Japan's Cabinet Order implementing the Road Traffic Act (1960), as revised effective 2026-09-01. It sets traffic signals, speed limits, vehicle loading, licensing and penalty-point rules. It includes provisions on remotely operated small vehicles (delivery robots) and a chapter on specific automated operation (Level 4 autonomous driving).",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Remotely operated small vehicles are treated as pedestrians for traffic signal purposes (Art. 2).",
   "Chapter 4-3 sets special rules for specific automated operation (Arts. 27-7, 27-8), including custody of damaged items after accidents.",
   "Stopped specific-automated-operation vehicles must show a prescribed stop-indicating device.",
   "Sets maximum speeds, driver licensing, penalty point and licence suspension standards.",
   "Defines walking-assist devices including motorised ones under Cabinet Office standards (Art. 1)."
  ],
